<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cormorant+Garamond:wght@500;600&family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

<style>
  .section-why-works {
    font-family: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', -apple-system, sans-serif;
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 48px auto;
    padding: 0 20px;
    color: #2a2a2a;
  }

  .section-why-works__header {
    font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 32px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #1a1a1a;
    margin: 0 0 32px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .section-why-works__image {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 500px;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 12px;
    margin: 0 auto 32px;
    display: block;
  }

  .section-why-works__body {
    max-width: 560px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .section-why-works__para {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    color: #2a2a2a;
  }

  .section-why-works__highlight {
    font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 22px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: #2d6b5d;
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin: 28px 0;
    padding: 20px 24px;
    border-left: 3px solid #2d6b5d;
    background: #f7f3ed;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .section-why-works {
      margin: 32px auto;
    }
    .section-why-works__header {
      font-size: 26px;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }
    .section-why-works__para {
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .section-why-works__highlight {
      font-size: 19px;
      padding: 16px 20px;
      margin: 24px 0;
    }
  }
</style>

<section class="section-why-works">
  <h2 class="section-why-works__header">Your skin isn't dry.<br>It's starving.</h2>

  {% comment %} REPLACE IMAGE_URL_HERE WITH TEXTURE SWATCH ON HAND IMAGE {% endcomment %}
  <img
    src="IMAGE_URL_HERE"
    alt="Tallow balm absorbing into skin"
    class="section-why-works__image"
  >

  <div class="section-why-works__body">
    <p class="section-why-works__para">
      Your skin makes a natural oil called sebum. It's what keeps your skin soft, hydrated, and protected.
    </p>

    <p class="section-why-works__para">
      After 40, your body produces up to 60% less of it. After menopause, it can drop even further.
    </p>

    <p class="section-why-works__para">
      That's why your moisturizer stopped working. It adds water. Your skin needs oil.
    </p>

    <p class="section-why-works__highlight">
      Your skin needs fats it actually recognizes.
    </p>

    <p class="section-why-works__para">
      Tallow is almost identical to the oil your skin makes on its own. When you apply it, your skin doesn't treat it like a foreign product sitting on top.
    </p>

    <p class="section-why-works__para">
      It absorbs it — because it recognizes it as its own.
    </p>

    <p class="section-why-works__para">
      That's the difference between a moisturizer that disappears by noon and one that lasts all day.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
